WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.580
Plants on one square metre fix 12,000 kilojoules in a year.

2
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.320
Why does so little of that energy reach the animals at the top?

3
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:16.330
These numbers come from a made-up budget for one year.

4
00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.710
Each one is a rate, energy per square metre per year.

5
00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:22.890
That is production.

6
00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:28.690
It is a flow, like deposits into an account, not the balance at one moment.

7
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:35.850
The plants' total fixation is called gross primary production The plants respire

8
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:37.450
part of it just to stay alive.

9
00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:41.710
In this budget it is half, and that half leaves as heat.

10
00:00:42.783 --> 00:00:48.383
What remains is net primary production It is all the energy left for everything

11
00:00:48.383 --> 00:00:50.323
else, to eat or to store.

12
00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:54.517
Now follow it up one feeding step, to the herbivores.

13
00:00:55.737 --> 00:00:58.497
At this step, every kilojoule has three ways out.

14
00:00:59.777 --> 00:01:00.777
Call them doors.

15
00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:06.187
The herbivores could eat most of the plants' production, or only a little of it.

16
00:01:07.287 --> 00:01:08.287
Which do you expect?

17
00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:16.510
Only a little, here less than a third.

18
00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.130
The rest is never eaten.

19
00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:23.750
It dies and drops through the brown door, into detritus.

20
00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:29.890
Detritus is dead matter that feeds bacteria, fungi and animals that eat it.

21
00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:34.380
Of what the herbivores eat, much passes straight through, as feces.

22
00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.060
That goes out the brown door too, into the same detritus.

23
00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:44.333
Of what they absorb, a large part is respired just to keep them alive.

24
00:01:45.693 --> 00:01:47.633
It leaves through the grey door, as heat.

25
00:01:48.717 --> 00:01:52.097
What is left becomes new herbivore tissue and offspring.

26
00:01:53.317 --> 00:01:56.617
That is the herbivores' production, passed up from the plants.

27
00:01:58.297 --> 00:02:00.597
Predators can eat it, but they do not eat all of it.

28
00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:05.090
Each door sets a fraction, drawn as a valve on the pipe.

29
00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:07.470
One is the share eaten.

30
00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:09.990
One is the share absorbed.

31
00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:12.910
One is the share made into tissue.

32
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.980
The three valves in a row give the share that reaches the herbivores.

33
00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:23.520
It is the product of the three fractions, called the trophic transfer efficiency.

34
00:02:24.683 --> 00:02:26.663
Nothing vanishes along the way.

35
00:02:27.943 --> 00:02:31.943
The three doors together account for every kilojoule that this step received.

36
00:02:33.203 --> 00:02:34.743
In this budget, the books close.

37
00:02:35.817 --> 00:02:38.997
At every step up, the same three doors open again.

38
00:02:40.117 --> 00:02:44.357
So the fractions multiply, and production shrinks fast up a food chain.

39
00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:51.350
This holds for rates over one period, in one currency, while consumers eat no more

40
00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:52.830
than the production below them.

41
00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:56.030
Energy never returns to the plants.

42
00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.550
It is stored for a while, or leaves as heat.
